{
  "_comment": [
    "Place naming as DATA (the same split as streets.json): the C++ (world/place_names.h) owns the",
    "algorithm, this file the words. Glenn, 2026-09-25: 'I'll leave it to you to generate the town",
    "names. They don't have to be Hawaiian.' A name is a ROOT + an ENDING run together (Ash + ford ->",
    "Ashford), and a place's SITE can shape it: a coastal town may be 'Port ...' or '... Bay', a town on",
    "a river '... Ford' or '...bridge', the mountain town '... Ridge'. Each word is used once per world",
    "while the banks last; the same world seed always gives the same names.",
    "routes: what the island's roads are signed as, and the two directions round a ring road (the",
    "Capital Beltway's convention: the INNER loop runs clockwise, the OUTER counter-clockwise)."
  ],
  "places": {
    "seed": 20260925,
    "roots": ["Ash", "Bram", "Clay", "Dun", "Elm", "Fair", "Glen", "Hart", "Ivy", "Kings", "Lark", "Marl",
              "Oak", "Pen", "Red", "Stan", "Thorn", "Wey", "Wick", "Alder", "Bel", "Carr", "Hol", "Mill",
              "Brook", "Cold", "Deer", "Fern", "Gold", "Hazel", "Lin", "Moss", "Ned", "Os", "Quarry",
              "Rook", "Salt", "Stone", "Swan", "Tarn", "Wren", "Yew", "Ember", "Grey", "Heath", "Kel"],
    "endings": ["ford", "field", "ton", "by", "wick", "stead", "ham", "well", "dale", "wood", "worth",
                "more", "ley", "bury", "holm", "combe", "hurst", "gate", "wyn", "sted"],
    "traits": {
      "coastal":  {"chance": 0.45, "prefix": ["Port "], "suffix": [" Bay", " Harbor", " Point", " Cove"],
                   "endings": ["mouth", "haven", "port", "cliff", "sands"]},
      "river":    {"chance": 0.5, "suffix": [" Falls", " Crossing"], "endings": ["ford", "bridge", "mouth", "water"]},
      "mountain": {"chance": 0.8, "suffix": [" Ridge", " Summit", " Heights"], "endings": ["crest", "top", "fell"]}
    },
    "cityChance": 0.25
  },
  "routes": {
    "freeway": "1",
    "pass": "2",
    "mountain": "3",
    "loop": {"clockwise": "Inner Loop", "counterclockwise": "Outer Loop"},
    "freewayName": "Route",
    "exitNumbering": "km"
  }
}
{
  "_comment": [
    "Street naming and sign look as DATA (Glenn, 2026-09-20: 'for the street names",
    "you've put them in code. I'm starting to wonder if some of this shouldn't be",
    "data and not baked into the C++'). The C++ owns the ALGORITHM -- which edges",
    "form one street (street_names.h) and how a blade is lettered to fit",
    "(street_signs.h). This file owns the CONTENT: the words, what suffix a road of",
    "a given width carries, how a sign shop shortens it, and what the blade looks",
    "like. Edit it and the city renames itself; no rebuild.",
    "A name is '<word> <suffix>'. Banks are drawn from evenly; a word is used once",
    "per city while the banks last."
  ],
  "names": {
    "seed": 20260918,
    "banks": {
      "trees": ["Oak", "Maple", "Elm", "Cedar", "Willow", "Birch", "Aspen", "Alder",
                "Chestnut", "Hawthorn", "Laurel", "Linden", "Magnolia", "Juniper",
                "Poplar", "Sycamore", "Hazel", "Rowan", "Spruce", "Walnut", "Cypress",
                "Hickory", "Locust", "Mulberry", "Pine", "Redwood", "Sequoia",
                "Tamarack", "Beech", "Dogwood"],
      "people": ["Lincoln", "Jefferson", "Franklin", "Madison", "Monroe", "Jackson",
                 "Harrison", "Sherman", "Grant", "Hamilton", "Adams", "Clay", "Kearny",
                 "Bryant", "Folsom", "Larkin", "Geary", "Taylor", "Hayes", "Fulton",
                 "Page", "Haight", "Mason", "Powell", "Stockton", "Davis", "Howard",
                 "Bancroft", "Lowell", "Emerson"],
      "places": ["Harbour", "Market", "Mill", "Quarry", "Foundry", "Cannery", "Depot",
                 "Union", "Commerce", "Exchange", "Granary", "Wharf", "Mission",
                 "Station", "College", "Church", "Garden", "Orchard", "Meadow", "Ridge",
                 "Summit", "Valley", "Lake", "River", "Bridge", "Park", "Hill", "Spring",
                 "Forest", "Canal"],
      "ordinals": ["First", "Second", "Third", "Fourth", "Fifth", "Sixth", "Seventh",
                   "Eighth", "Ninth", "Tenth", "Eleventh", "Twelfth", "Thirteenth",
                   "Fourteenth", "Fifteenth", "Sixteenth", "Seventeenth", "Eighteenth",
                   "Nineteenth", "Twentieth"]
    },
    "suffixes": [
      { "minWidth": 16, "choices": ["Boulevard", "Avenue", "Parkway"] },
      { "minWidth": 13, "choices": ["Avenue", "Road", "Way"] },
      { "minWidth": 9,  "choices": ["Street", "Road", "Drive"] },
      { "minWidth": 0,  "choices": ["Lane", "Court", "Place"] }
    ],
    "classSuffix": { "alley": "Alley" },
    "abbreviations": {
      "Boulevard": "Blvd", "Parkway": "Pkwy", "Avenue": "Ave", "Street": "St",
      "Road": "Rd", "Drive": "Dr", "Lane": "Ln", "Court": "Ct", "Place": "Pl",
      "Alley": "Aly", "Way": "Way"
    }
  },
  "signs": {
    "_comment": "Metres, except the atlas sizes (pixels) and the fractions.",
    "bladeHeight": 0.30,
    "minBladeWidth": 0.75,
    "maxBladeWidth": 1.8,
    "topBladeY": 3.05,
    "bladeStep": 0.34,
    "kerbGap": 1.0,
    "bladePx": 80,
    "pagePx": 2048,
    "capFraction": 0.56,
    "capFloorFraction": 0.40,
    "face": [0, 104, 64],
    "legend": [246, 246, 240]
  }
}
